<title>SWITZERLAND: Oerlikon forecasts higher 1996 profit.</title>
<headline>Oerlikon forecasts higher 1996 profit.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swiss technology and consumer goods group Oerlikon-Buehrle Holding AG said it expects its 1996 net income to be considerably higher than in 1995, but it will not be as high as the 75 million Swiss francs achieved in 1994.</p>
<p>The company also said orders received and gross sales were down slightly during the first 10 months of 1996 compared to the same period last year following the sale of several companies.</p>
<p>But the operating result and net income have improved significantly.</p>
<p>Orders received during the period were down 2.7 percent to 2.8 billion francs and gross sales were down 1.8 percent during the 10-month period to 2.9 bilion, the company also said.</p>
<p>--Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
